---
title: Theming
description: Light/dark mode and accent color presets.
order: 5
---

Theming is class-based: adding `.dark` to `<html>` swaps every CSS variable in `app.css` to its dark-mode value. The toggle in the site header flips this class and persists the choice to `localStorage`; a small inline script in `app.html` reads that value before the page paints, so there's no flash of the wrong theme on load.

## Accent colors

On top of the base neutral theme, a `data-accent` attribute on `<html>` (Default, Amber, or Violet) overrides just the accent-relevant tokens — `--primary`, `--ring`, `--sidebar-primary`, `--sidebar-ring` — for both light and dark. The palette dropdown next to the light/dark toggle switches it, persisted to `localStorage` under `accent-theme` and applied by the same no-flash boot script as the light/dark choice.

Add a new preset by adding a `:root[data-accent="<id>"]`/`:root.dark[data-accent="<id>"]` pair to `app.css` and an entry to `accentThemes` in `src/lib/accent-theme.ts`.
